\b AutoGAD for AutoCAD\b0\par
\par
AutoGAD is an AI assistant that runs inside AutoCAD. By installing it you agree to the following.\par
\par
\b 1. Anthropic API key required.\b0  AutoGAD does not include AI access. Each user must supply their own Anthropic API key. Usage is billed to that key by Anthropic under their terms at https://www.anthropic.com/legal/consumer-terms.\par
\par
\b 2. Drawing data leaves your machine.\b0  When you ask a question, information about the active drawing - including layer names, block names, schedule and table text, entity properties, and text you type - is sent to the Anthropic API for processing. Do not use AutoGAD with drawings whose contents you are not permitted to transmit to a third-party service.\par
\par
\b 3. AutoGAD can modify your drawings.\b0  It can change layer states, edit text, run commands, and alter drawing properties. Each such action asks for confirmation, but you remain responsible for reviewing the results. Save and back up your work.\par
\par
\b 4. AI output can be wrong.\b0  Calculations, quantities, and engineering advice produced by AutoGAD must be independently verified by a qualified professional before being relied upon. AutoGAD is not a substitute for professional judgement and does not certify any design.\par
\par
\b 5. No warranty.\b0  This software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or implied, including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and non-infringement. To the maximum extent permitted by law, the authors are not liable for any claim, damages, data loss, or other liability arising from the software or its use.\par
\par
\b 6. Trademarks.\b0  AutoCAD and Autodesk are trademarks of Autodesk, Inc. Claude and Anthropic are trademarks of Anthropic, PBC. AutoGAD is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by either company.\par
